  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TASUWORI established in 2014, Tanzania Support for Women Rights (TASUWORI) is a non-governmental and non-profit organisation working to uphold youth both female and male in Tanzania. The organisation focuses on improving the living standard of youth, women and children. As part of these efforts, the organisation works to ensure that young people are empowered to make decisions about their lives. Since inception in 2014, TASUWORI has been working to support the effort made by youth both male and female inensuring that the group is socially and economically empowered. TASUWORI have established Self help groups in which youth are their major target. About 10 groups has been established with 20-25 members each In Morogoro Municipal and Gairo District.  TASUWORI have enhanced capacity of youth in the Agriculture value chain particularly in the subsectors of horticulture, poultry keeping, entrepreneurship and Sack garden horticulture practices. With this project the organization is positioned to use its youthmobilization experience to bring together this group of hard to reach in ensuring that they participate in decision making in their villages and wards.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tanzania Support for Women#s Rights</narrative>
